Include GL/gl.h next to GL/glx.h in headers

libx11-compat ships a trimmed GL/glx.h that, unlike Mesa's, does not pull in
GL/gl.h (so GLES clients need no desktop GL headers). Open Inventor's headers
that include only GL/glx.h, and the code built on them, rely on that implicit
gl.h (GLenum, gl* entry points), so include it explicitly.

diff --git a/apps/samples/widgets/MyTextureEditor.h b/apps/samples/widgets/MyTextureEditor.h
index bba06a6..af60436 100644
--- a/apps/samples/widgets/MyTextureEditor.h
+++ b/apps/samples/widgets/MyTextureEditor.h
@@ -60,6 +60,7 @@
 
 #include <X11/Intrinsic.h>
 #include <Xm/Xm.h>
+#include <GL/gl.h>
 #include <GL/glx.h>
 #include <Inventor/Xt/SoXtComponent.h>
 #include <Inventor/misc/SoCallbackList.h>
